# Boreal demo reel: 30 s at 60 fps, 1280x720.
#
#   build/brtest --film 1800 --size 1280x720 --script docs/demo.cues \
#     | ffmpeg -f rawvideo -pix_fmt rgba -s 1280x720 -r 60 -i - -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p -crf 18 docs/demo.mp4
#
# Tracks are held before their first key and interpolated between keys, so a
# button press is three keys (0, 1, 0).

# The defaults, a little faster than real time.
0     Speed            0.625
# A substorm at 4 s: the sheet strength jumps, the poleward arc brightens and surges west.
239   Substorm         0
240   Substorm         1
241   Substorm         0
# Swing up under the arcs to the magnetic zenith (south, 77 degrees up).
600   Look Elevation   0.35
600   Look Azimuth     0.5
600   Oval Distance    0.425
600   Field of View    0.5556
900   Look Elevation   0.87
900   Look Azimuth     1.0
900   Oval Distance    0.3
900   Field of View    0.78
# The whole sky, as an all-sky camera records it.
1080  Camera           0
1081  Camera           1
# Solar maximum, softer electrons: the red line rises and lingers.
1200  Activity         0.4
1200  Energy           0.588
1440  Activity         1.0
1440  Energy           0.25
# Back to a rectilinear view, then the same sky as the dark-adapted eye sees it.
1500  Camera           1
1501  Camera           0
1500  Look Elevation   0.87
1501  Look Elevation   0.35
1500  Look Azimuth     1.0
1501  Look Azimuth     0.5
1500  Field of View    0.78
1501  Field of View    0.5556
1650  Observer         0
1651  Observer         1
